RF.put("questb:b64",{"8544":{"id":8544,"t":"Conqueror's Spaulders","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of Night, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Neutral reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nQiraji Bindings of Command Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Night Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"It is said among us that the ornate shoulder armor worn by the mortal races started as an attempt to emulate the wings of a dragon.\nBring me the bindings worn by the highest Qiraji leaders and I shall shape them into a set of pauldrons more dreadful than even the wings of Nefarian himself!","rew":"You will receive:\nConqueror's Spaulders\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Have you collected the components I require?","done":"From the materials you bring and from the scales of our fallen Qiraji foes I make you these pauldrons, mortal. May they grant you the protection you need and may the sight of them strike fear into our enemies.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Warrior Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8544\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Conqueror's Spaulders this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of Night, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8784":{"id":8784,"t":"Secrets of the Qiraji","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Ancient Qiraji Artifact to the dragons hiding near the entrance of the temple.\nAncient Qiraji Artifact Vekniss Warrior 9.2 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Soldier 7.7 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 7.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Wasp 6.3 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nProvided: Ancient Qiraji Artifact","desc":"You have discovered an ancient Qiraji artifact! Perhaps one of the dragons near the entrance of the temple would have a use for this relic.","back":"You're glowing! I know what that means...","done":"An exceptional find, ‹name›. Simply marvelous! This will definitely give us some insight into our enemy's twisted minds.\nStart an item: Ancient Qiraji Artifact End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8784","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8704":{"id":8704,"t":"Signet of the Unseen Path","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Ceremonial Ring, 2 Amber Idols, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Windcaller Yessendra in Silithus. You must also attain Honored reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Ceremonial Ring Ayamiss the Hunter 30 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ossirian the Unscarred 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , General Rajaxx 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 2 more\n2 Amber Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The rings worn by the Qiraji lieutenants are rumored to grant them formidable abilities. The corrupted gems that adorn them could, in theory, be swapped out with more pure materials to create uncorrupted versions of the rings.\nThe gems that adorn Qiraji idols would work quite well, as their quality is superior.\nBring me the ring and idols and I'll create a powerful ring for you, ‹class›.","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet of the Unseen Path\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the ring and materials, ‹name›?","done":"I will swap the gem on the ring for you. You'll find the effect is much more... agreeable.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Windcaller Yessendra","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8624":{"id":8624,"t":"Stormcaller's Leggings","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Skin of the Great Sandworm, 2 Idols of Strife, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nSkin of the Great Sandworm Ouro\n2 Idol of Strife Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"You seek to prove your worth to my kind, mortal? Very well, perhaps we can be of mutual assistance.\nThe ancient sandworm, Ouro, is a being of legendary power. He is rumored to have been created by the Old God himself as a mockery of life.\nHis skin is unnatural... thick, nearly impregnable, yet it's flexible and allows him to move with the speed and grace of a much smaller creature.\nBring me a sample of his skin along with other minor components and I shall craft you leggings of great power.","rew":"You will receive:\nStormcaller's Leggings\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You've acquired the items I requested, ‹name›?\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Horde Class Shaman Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8624\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Stormcaller's Leggings this quest\nBring the Skin of the Great Sandworm, 2 Idols of Strife, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8384":{"id":8384,"t":"Claiming Arathi Basin","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Winning a war is about more than just outsmarting and outfighting your opponent. Victory often comes down to simply producing more than your enemy.\nWhat we have in Arathi Basin is a sizeable supply of resources for whichever side manages to claim it first.\nIf the Alliance comes out victorious, it'll mean more swords and pikes for our troops. If the Horde were to win, those swords and pikes would still get made, they'd just be pointed at us! Now is the time to help the Alliance in Arathi Basin, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with The League of Arathor","back":"Tell me, what are the news from the front?","done":"Good work, soldier! Keep it up and we'll have the Horde running all the way back to Orgrimmar.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"1024":{"id":1024,"t":"Raene's Cleansing","lv":21,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Shael'dryn at the moonwell to the northeast.\nGlowing Gem Saltspittle Oracle 10 % , Saltspittle Muckdweller 10 % , Saltspittle Warrior 10 % , Saltspittle Puddlejumper 10 %\nProvided: Glowing Gem","desc":"You'll have to do the research yourself, but from what notes Teronis has made, it sounds like your next course of action is to find the other pieces of the rod Dartol created. I would start by heading to the moonwell east of Iris Lake. When you're ready, follow the road and turn north when you reach a small sitting area on your left.\nA dryad there named Shael'dryn is better suited to guide you. Seek her out.\nKeep the gem with you--Shael'dryn will need it if she's to help you recreate the rod.","rew":"Experience: 825\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Hello. How are you?","done":"Oh, Raene sent you? It must be serious indeed. What can I help you with?","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":36.6,"y":49.6,"n":"Raene Wolfrunner","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":53.5,"y":46.2,"n":"Shael'dryn","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"6544":{"id":6544,"t":"Torek's Assault","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort Torek on his attack against Silverwing Outpost and Duriel Moonfire, then report to Ertog Ragetusk at Splintertree Post.","desc":"Hey! ‹class›! Come here!\nMy raiders and I are about to attack the Silverwing Outpost to the west. Our target is its leader, Duriel Moonfire. Scouts report the outpost is defended heavily with sentinels and warriors. The battle will be glorious!\nDo you want to share in the glory, ‹name›, and aid us? If so, then when it's over you can report our success to my superior, Ertog Ragetusk in Splintertree.\nWhat do you say. Are you with us?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPolished Walking Staff Slatemetal Cutlass\nMoney: 17 0 gold, 17 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,400\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Torek was sent on a mission against Silverwing Outpost. Was the attack successful?","done":"So Torek's attack was successful! Well done, ‹name›. Night elves are decent foes. A little skinny, but strong and fierce! I'm sure the battle was something to see...\nAnd I hope you gained a scar or two!","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":68.3,"y":75.3,"n":"Torek","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":73,"y":62.5,"n":"Ertog Ragetusk","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"2784":{"id":2784,"t":"Fall From Grace","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Listen to the Fallen Hero of the Horde tell his story.","desc":"Hear my story, ‹race›.","rew":"Experience: 470","back":"Listen to what I have to say.","done":"As a spirit, I am powerless, ‹name›. Assist me. Allow me to regain my honor.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"3824":{"id":3824,"t":"Gor'tesh the Brute Lord","lv":53,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Gor'tesh, somewhere to the west of Dreadmaul Rock. Kill Gor'tesh and then take Gor'tesh's Lopped Off Head back to Oralius in Burning Steppes.\nGor'tesh's Lopped Off Head Gor'tesh","desc":"They're reeling I tell you! Our next strike must be decisive.\nThe brute lord, Gor'tesh, must be slain. More importantly, his head must be returned to me so that I may prepare the third phase of our attack on the Firegut ogres.\nBe warned, soldier, Gor'tesh rules not from Dreadmaul Rock but from a Blackrock orc structure to the west of Dreadmaul Rock.\nYour orders, then, are simple. Find Gor'tesh and chop off his fat head. Return to me when the job is done.\nSHUT UP, WINKY!","rew":"Experience: 5,250\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Oh glorious day! Have you returned with the head?","done":"Just look at it, soldier. Disgusting! When the remaining Firegut ogres see this fat mug stuck on a pike sitting at the top of their mountain, mass hysteria will ensue!\n<Oralius cackles wildly.>","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.6,"y":68.7,"n":"Oralius","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"4224":{"id":4224,"t":"The True Masters","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Ragged John to learn of Marshal Windsor's fate and return to Marshal Maxwell when you have completed this task.\nYou recall Marshal Maxwell telling you to search for him in a cave to the north.","desc":"What? You thought you were the first? How many soldiers must we lose before Stormwind acts?\nWe had accumulated enormous amounts of intelligence pertaining to the Blackrock menace before we lost our commanding officer, Marshal Windsor. With Marshal Windsor went all of our precious information.\nWhat we need is that documentation. Speak with Ragged John, ‹name›. He was with Windsor when they were attacked by a Blackrock raiding party. He was last seen in a cave to the north.","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"Have you spoken with John yet?","done":"I could have warned you, but what fun is that?","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.7,"y":69,"n":"Marshal Maxwell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"97904":{"id":97904,"t":"Camping 101 fishing","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Lau'Tiki near Sen'jin Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your fishing skill to 20","desc":"You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.","back":"I can teach you once you've gained some skill as a fisherman.","done":"Dere ya have it, ya be craftin' your very own Fish Bowl. Most folk don't be carin' much for camps being set up in da center of town, so ya be needin' ta head into da wilderness if ya be wantin' to try it out.\nNo camp is complete without a campfire, mon. Ya be needin' one of dose before ya be startin' up your camp. Most cooks be teachin' ya ta make a fire. Check in with someone who can train ya in da culinary arts if ya haven't already learned da basics.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":47.4,"n":"Brakk","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":53.2,"y":81.4,"n":"Lau'Tiki","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94224":{"id":94224,"t":"Craftsmans writ heavy bronze mace","min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Heavy Bronze Mace\nHeavy Bronze Mace","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Heavy Bronze Mace, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Shh. Keep your voice down. I'm not ready for a fight, yet.","done":"Whoa. You came well prepared! Hope that mace is for me, unless you plan to do ALL of the fighting.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":80,"y":48.2,"n":"Gorgrash","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94304":{"id":94304,"t":"Craftsmans writ mageweave bag","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Mageweave Bag\nMageweave Bag","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Mageweave Bag, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Mageweave Bag Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94304","cats":["crafting"]},"944":{"id":944,"t":"The Master's Glaive","lv":17,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather information, then use the Phial of Scrying to create a Scrying Bowl. Use the bowl to speak with Onu.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.\nProvided: Phial of Scrying","desc":"It is strange that the naga are here, in Darkshore. But stranger still...are the Twilight's Hammer. That cult worships the old, old lords of the earth. Lords defeated long ago.\nThe Master's Glaive, to the south, is a place where such an old lord fell.\nGo there and look for more Twilight's Hammer cultists.\nTake this phial of scrying. Use it to create a scrying bowl after searching the Master's Glaive. Then speak to me through the bowl.","rew":"Experience: 625\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The Master's Glaive, ‹name›.\nGo there, then speak with me again.","done":"The Twilight's Hammer is at the Master's Glaive?\nUnfortunate.\nThe old lord impaled by the glaive is long dead, but that does not mean slivers of his power do not still remain.\nThe Twilight's Hammer must be seeking this power.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":43.6,"y":76.3,"n":"Onu","s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"7504":{"id":7504,"t":"Holy Bologna: What the Light Won't Tell You","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 7,050, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Return the book to its rightful owners.\nHoly Bologna: What the Light Won't Tell You A Dusty Tome 0 % , A Dusty Tome 0 %\nProvided: Holy Bologna: What the Light Won't Tell You","desc":"The tome carries the mark of the Athenaeum.","rew":"You will receive:\nRoyal Seal of Eldre'Thalas\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"You have recovered a tome!","done":"Excellent work, ‹race›. Should you find any more tomes, do not hesitate to return them to us.\nAs time passes, we tend to change around and even add new rewards for the return of missing tomes.\nStart an item: Holy Bologna: What the Light Won't Tell You End Lorekeeper Javon Level 60 , requires level 54 Difficulty 54 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Class Priest Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 7504","cats":["dire-maul"]},"384":{"id":384,"t":"Beer Basted Boar Ribs","lv":7,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Ragnar Thunderbrew in Kharanos wants 6 Crag Boar Ribs and a mug of Rhapsody Malt.\n6 Crag Boar Rib Large Crag Boar 52.8 % , Crag Boar 52.4 % , Elder Crag Boar 50.9 % , Scarred Crag Boar 46.1 % and 1 more\nRhapsody Malt sold by Innkeeper Belm , sold by Yanni Stoutheart , sold by Innkeeper Thulfram","desc":"Nothing my tavern patrons enjoy more than some Beer Basted Boar Ribs! Only problem is, the local trapper who used to bring me supplies enlisted in the King's Army to help with the war on the Alliance front.\nMaybe you can help me out? If you bring me six crag boar ribs and a Rhapsody Malt from the tavern here, I'll give you the family recipe for my famous Beer Basted Boar Ribs, not to mention a free sample! The secret's in the Malt!","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Beer Basted Boar Ribs Recipe: Beer Basted Boar Ribs\nMoney: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"I'm going to need six crag boar ribs and a mug of Rhapsody Malt, ‹name›.","done":"The Malt is brewed, the Boars are dead\nAnd before all is done and anything said\nWe will have to fight for first dibs\nOn these savory Beer Basted Boar Ribs!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.8,"y":52.4,"n":"Ragnar Thunderbrew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"7664":{"id":7664,"t":"Ivory Raptor Replacement","lv":1,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Whistle of the Ivory Raptor","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSwift Blue Raptor Swift Olive Raptor Swift Orange Raptor","back":"You bring me your old raptor, I give you new one with freshly sharpened claws! The new raptor will be just as fast as your old one, but with a new look to him. You can look at the swift raptors here to see what you will have to choose from.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":55.2,"y":75.6,"n":"Zjolnir","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"784":{"id":784,"t":"Vanquish the Betrayers","lv":7,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Kul Tiras Sailors, 8 Kul Tiras Marines and Lieutenant Benedict and return to Gar'Thok in Razor Hill.\nKul Tiras Sailor slain : 0/ 10\nKul Tiras Marine slain : 0/ 8\nLieutenant Benedict slain","desc":"Led by Admiral Proudmoore, the humans of Kul Tiras encroached on Durotar, violating the Warchief's pact made with Jaina Proudmoore in order to defeat Archimonde years ago.\nThe human aggression was repelled and Tiragarde Keep fell. But recently, the Admiral's reserves, led by Lieutenant Benedict, have retaken the keep and once again pose a threat to our homeland. These humans show no respect for diplomacy.\nProve your honor and travel south to Tiragarde Keep to eliminate the human invaders.","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"You have your orders, ‹name›. The safety of Durotar is in question. Complete the task before you or hang your head in shame.\nShow your honor and defeat the humans of Tiragarde Keep.","done":"Word of your bravery travels fast, ‹class›. Tales of your victory at Tiragarde Keep will be heralded in Orgrimmar.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":51.9,"y":43.5,"n":"Gar'Thok","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"9184":{"id":9184,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Wicked Leather Headband","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 10 Wicked Leather Headbands and the Craftsman's Writ - Wicked Leather Headband - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Wicked Leather Headband\n10 Wicked Leather Headband\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Wicked Leather Headband","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order LW-971:\n10 Wicked Leather Headbands.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"These are... wicked.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9664":{"id":9664,"t":"Establishing New Outposts","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Capture Crown Guard Tower, Eastwall Tower, Northpass Tower and Plaguewood Tower in the Eastern Plaguelands, then return to Emmisary Whitebeard at Light's Hope Chapel.\nCapture Crown Guard Tower\nCapture Eastwall Tower\nCapture Northpass Tower\nCapture Plaguewood Tower","desc":"Welcome to the Plaguelands, ‹name›. As you know, the Forsaken and their allies hold the lands to the west of here against our best efforts. The Alliance commanders have decided that here in the east, we will establish new fortifications to tighten the noose around our enemies.\nTowers long abandoned since the days of Lordaeron are to be seized and rebuilt for this purpose. These lands are dangerous, and we could use your help.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600","back":"When the towers are under our control, we will soon be able to surround the Forsaken. After that, it is only a matter of time before we can crush them.","done":"Very good, ‹name›. It will be important for us to hold these towers against future attacks, and for that we may need your assistance until reinforcements can be brought in to secure the area.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.5,"y":49.7,"n":"Emmisary Whitebeard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"5264":{"id":5264,"t":"Lord Maxwell Tyrosus","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Lord Maxwell Tyrosus. He is inside the church.","desc":"I am about to bestow a great honor upon you, ‹name›.\nLord Maxwell wishes to reward you for your service to the Argent Dawn!\nIt has been years since Maxwell has granted audience to outsiders.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","done":"You are a worthy ally, ‹name›. You shall reap the rewards of your stalwart dedication.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":50.1,"n":"Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.9,"y":48.4,"n":"Lord Maxwell Tyrosus","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"6144":{"id":6144,"t":"The Call to Command","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 650 experience instead of 675, 0.96 times as much.","obj":"Travel to the Undercity and speak with Varimathras.","desc":"The order has come down, ‹class›. Varimathras himself has requested that I send my most 'capable' agents back to the Undercity for a highly sensitive tactical operation.\nUnfortunately, my most capable agents were killed over three years ago. In their stead I have a collection of brain dead riff-raff.\n<Nathanos stares coldly at you.>\nTravel to the Undercity at once and report to Varimathras. Do not embarrass me, ‹class›!","rew":"Experience: 650\n+10 reputation with Undercity","done":"The Grand Crusader sits safely in the Scarlet Bastion while his forces pour into your lands, desecrate your structures and monuments and murder your people.\nThe Dark Lady has commanded that I deal with this insect once and for all. You will become the instrument of the Forsaken's reckoning.\nEastern Plaguelands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":22.2,"y":63.5,"n":"Nathanos Blightcaller","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":56.3,"y":92.2,"n":"Varimathras","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"3904":{"id":3904,"t":"Milly's Harvest","lv":4,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 crates of Milly's Harvest to Milly Osworth at Northshire Abbey.\n8 Milly's Harvest Milly's Harvest","desc":"A gang of brigands, the Defias, moved into the Northshire Vineyards while I was harvesting! I reported it to the Northshire guards and they assured me they'd take care of things, but... I'm afraid for my crop of grapes! If the Defias don't steal them then I fear our guards will trample them when they chase away the thugs.\nPlease, you must help me! I gathered most of my grapes into buckets, but I left them in the vineyards to the southeast.\nBring me those buckets! Save my harvest!","rew":"Experience: 180\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Do you have my harvest, ‹name›?","done":"Oh thank you, ‹name›! You saved my harvest! And I hope you showed a few of those Defias that they can't cause trouble around here.\nWe might be short on guards these days, but we're lucky to have heroes like you to protect us!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":50.7,"y":39.3,"n":"Milly Osworth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"95664":{"id":95664,"t":"Elder knowledge","lv":31,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Take the Titan Relic to the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff and look for someone who can tell you more about it.\nTitan Relic","desc":"This unusual composite shard scatters light like a living prism. Its nature is uncertain, but its power feels ancient. The most knowledgeable minds for artifacts of this bygone age must reside on the Elder rise in Thunder Bluff.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":70.8,"y":33.8,"n":"Bashana Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["excavation-site-wetlands-dungeon"]},"4464":{"id":4464,"t":"Corrupted Songflower","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a songflower plant. A pungent, unhealthy odor emanates from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply some Cenarion plant salve to the songflower. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":48.3,"y":75.7,"n":"Corrupted Songflower","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"8464":{"id":8464,"t":"Winterfall Activity","lv":58,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Salfa wants you to kill 8 Winterfall Shaman, 8 Winterfall Den Watchers, and 8 Winterfall Ursa. Salfa is located just outside the entrance to Timbermaw Hold in Winterspring.\nWinterfall Shaman slain : 0/ 8\nWinterfall Den Watcher slain : 0/ 8\nWinterfall Ursa slain : 0/ 8","desc":"The Timbermaw tend to stay to themselves, ‹name›. While we do allow safe passage to those we trust, we try to avoid other furbolg tribes if at all possible.\nThe Winterfall tribe as of late has become increasingly hostile towards us. They seem to be in a state of rage, completely engulfed by their own fear and hatred of anything they do not understand.\nI must ask you to thin their numbers as to lessen the threat against us. Seek them out in Winterfall Village, far to the east of here.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEarth Warder's Gloves Gloves of the Pathfinder Vest of the Den Watcher Ursa's Embrace\nExperience: 6,200\n+150 reputation with Timbermaw Hold","back":"We very much appreciate what you have done for the Timbermaw, ‹name›. Your continued efforts will surely earn my tribe's trust and respect.","done":"Thank you for what you have done, as saddening as it is. Accept this as a token of thanks.\nI would ask of you to please continue helping us, ‹name›. We have very few allies on which to call upon, and without your aid, the threats against my tribe would surely be too much for us to handle alone.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":27.7,"y":34.5,"n":"Salfa","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"2944":{"id":2944,"t":"The Super Snapper FX","lv":48,"min":42,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Super Snapper FX to take a snapshot of Gammerita, then return to Daryn Lightwind in Rut'theran Village.\nSnapshot of Gammerita\nSuper Snapper FX\nProvided: Super Snapper FX","desc":"Have the first look at my new invention, ‹name›. All you need to do is target whatever it is you'd like to take a picture of, and push the button.\nWhat was that creature from the Hinterlands that you mentioned? Gammerita? Well, good luck finding her. I'm sure Daryn will be quite pleased with the snapshot you return to her.\nIn any case, here's the Super Snapper. Have fun!","rew":"Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"So, you have finally returned, ‹name›. And you've brought the contraption that Curgle built for me -- perfect.","done":"Well! Curgle's invention lived up to its expectations.\nDon't get too excited, but do know that I am pleased with your work, ‹name›.\nNow, where did I leave that book...\nTanaris Teldrassil The Hinterlands","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.4,"y":26.9,"n":"Curgle Cranklehop","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.4,"y":92.2,"n":"Daryn Lightwind","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"6624":{"id":6624,"t":"Triage","lv":45,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Save patients by using Triage Bandages to tend to their wounds. You must save 15 patients before 6 of them die from their injuries.\nRemember the order of triage! Critically Injured Soldiers die the fastest followed by Badly Injured Soldiers. Injured Soldiers take the longest to die and should be saved AFTER your Critically Injured and Badly Injured Soldiers have been triaged.\nProvided: Triage Bandage","desc":"Good day, doctor. You will be tested on your ability to triage patients accordingly this afternoon. Should you pass your examination, you will join the prestigious ranks of Alliance Trauma.\nNow pay attention! The critically injured must be tended to first. After the criticals come the badly injured. The injured should be tended to last. You must save 15 patients to pass this exam. You will fail should 6 of your patients die in triage.\nGood luck, doctor.","rew":"You will learn: First Aid\nExperience: 3,900","back":"Miraculous work, doctor. Simply miraculous.","done":"Doctor ‹name›, welcome to Alliance Trauma.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":67.8,"y":49,"n":"Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["first-aid"]},"8224":{"id":8224,"t":"Rare Fish - Dezian Queenfish","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 0. Pays 23s instead of 0.","obj":"Dezian Queenfish","rew":"You will receive:\nHigh Test Eternium Fishing Line\nMoney: 23 0 gold, 23 silver, 0 copper","back":"*Whir* *Click*\nI seek rare fish for Fishmaster Bluegill to catalogue. If you bring me a Dezian Queenfish, I will provide you with this fine reward.\n*Zzzap* *Whir*","done":"*Whir*\nIdentification of Dezian Queenfish complete.\nYour Reward is now available.\n*click-click* *Bzzzz*","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.3,"y":76.9,"n":"Fishbot 5000","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["fishing"]},"544":{"id":544,"t":"Prison Break In","lv":34,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the traitors and recover their artifacts, then return to Magus Voidglare in Tarren Mill.\nBloodstone Wedge Dermot\nBloodstone Marble Ricter\nBloodstone Shard Alina\nBloodstone Oval Kegan Darkmar","desc":"I came to Tarren Mill to research, but now must resolve a crisis. You see, four Forsaken fled the Undercity a few months ago. They turned their backs on their brethren, but what's worse...they stole from the Dark Lady.\nThese thieves broke into a secure vault and stole four artifacts, items our apothecaries required in certain studies. Sylvanas would have these artifacts returned.\nThe thieves fled the Undercity to Dalaran, and those wizards quarantined them in the Lordamere Internment Camp.","rew":"Money: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,350\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"Did you find the thieves? And more importantly, did you find what they stole?","done":"You have done a great service for the Forsaken, ‹name›. These artifacts have been sorely missed.\nAnd it is good to hear that Kegan and the other betrayers have found justice.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.6,"y":20.8,"n":"Magus Wordeen Voidglare","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6064":{"id":6064,"t":"Taming the Beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame a Large Crag Boar. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Grif Wildheart in Kharanos.\nTaming Rod\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"Hi there, lad/lass! So, you'd be wanting to know how you can gain a pet of your own?\nWell, let's get started. There's nothing more important than yer equipment when it comes to hunting, but we can chat about my new Shrapnel Blaster some other time. Fer now, let's focus on something I'm sure you're quite interested in: a pet!\nThe best way to learn is for you to try out several creatures as companions and see what ya like. So, find a large crag boar, then use the taming rod to tame it.","rew":"Experience: 850","back":"Don't worry, lad/lass! You'll get ta try a few before you'll need to decide on just one.","done":"I know, I know; you're wondering what's next, aren't ya?!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":45.8,"y":53,"n":"Grif Wildheart","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"94864":{"id":94864,"t":"Taming the beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame a Young Forest Bear. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Josephine Carson.\nTame a Young Forest Bear\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"You've proven yourself by taming a boar and a wolf, now it's time for your final challenge. Elwynn's balance depends on respect and skill. Take this Taming Rod and seek out a Young Forest Bear. Show that you can earn the trust of even the mightiest companion.\nCompleting this lesson will deepen your attunement to beasts.","back":"Go forth, Darlin, and tame the burliest of Elwynn beasts.","done":"The brawn of the forest. Brave work, Darlin!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.2,"y":66.2,"n":"Josephine Carson","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"9264":{"id":9264,"t":"Investigate the Scourge of Thunder Bluff","lv":10,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 625 experience instead of 650, 0.96 times as much.","obj":"Collect three Dim Necrotic Stones from the Scourge outside Thunder Bluff and investigate the glowing runic circles near their encampment.\n3 Dim Necrotic Stone Skeletal Soldier 35 % , Spectral Apparition 35 % , Spectral Spirit 31 % , Skeletal Trooper 31 %","desc":"The Lich King has sent his undead upon our very doorstep; we cannot remain idle! Surely you will step up to defend Thunder Bluff from these accursed invaders?\nThere are strange runic circles outside, glowing with the same energy that surrounds the undead and the Necropolis above. They have significance, I'm certain, and I want you to find out what. Thin the numbers of those aberrations while you're at it; bring me proof of their death along with your results, and I will reward you. Go!","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625","back":"Have you investigated the invasion yet? There's no time for dawdling!","done":"Hmm. From what you've told me, the voices within the circles... they must be used for communication of some kind. I shudder to think what unnatural minds are contacted through such magic. Regardless, you seem to have emerged whole and sane. The Argent Dawn appreciates your service.\nThunder Bluff Elwynn Forest Tirisfal Glades Dun Morogh Mulgore Durotar Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":31.1,"y":71.4,"n":"Lieutenant Lisande","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"224":{"id":224,"t":"In Defense of the King's Lands","lv":12,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Mountaineer Cobbleflint of the southern guard tower wants you to kill 10 Stonesplinter Troggs and 10 Stonesplinter Scouts.\nStonesplinter Trogg slain : 0/ 10\nStonesplinter Scout slain : 0/ 10","desc":"We need to protect the Loch, ‹name›! With so many of the King's soldiers fighting valiantly on remote battlefields, we've become overwhelmed on the home front. Troggs are tunneling up from every crevice! The Trogg infestation poses the largest threat to Ironforge. These disgusting mutants must be destroyed.\nWe need you, brave adventurer, to venture forth and lay waste to the Trogg threat. Slay 10 Stonesplinter Troggs and 10 Stonesplinter Scouts and report back.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Dalaran Sharp\nMoney: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Loch Modan is under siege, ‹name›! We need every able-bodied member of the Alliance to aid our cause. Have you killed 10 Stonesplinter Troggs and 10 Stonesplinter Scouts yet?","done":"Well done, ‹name›! You demonstrated uncanny courage on the battlefield. Our war against the Troggs will be won with efforts such as yours. You have served King Magni well.\nIf you fancy yourself well-suited for this kind of adventuring, I suggest you speak with Mountaineer Gravelgaw. The Captain has him assigned to a rough patrol that I am sure he can use some help with. Check with Gravelgaw just inside the tower.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":22.1,"y":73.1,"n":"Mountaineer Cobbleflint","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8864":{"id":8864,"t":"Festive Lunar Dresses","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Coin of Ancestry","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFestive Green Dress Festive Pink Dress Festive Purple Dress\nYou will also receive:\nLunar Festival Fireworks Pack","back":"I have a selection of dresses that may be of interest to you. Such dresses have been worn in times past during the Lunar Festival, and the selection I have today is perhaps the finest I have ever seen. Each is hand-crafted with only the finest and softest of components.\nIn exchange for some coins of ancestry, I will let you choose one of the three styles I have to keep as your own. Is this acceptable to you?","done":"Very well then - I accept these coins of ancestry. Please take your dress with my blessing. Also, please enjoy these complimentary fireworks.\nAs you have honored your elders, you honor me with your mere presence. Thank you, and may your Lunar Festival be joyous.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":53.7,"y":35.3,"n":"Valadar Starsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"3104":{"id":3104,"t":"Glyphic Letter","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Glyphic Letter and speak to Khelden Bremen inside Northshire Abbey.\nGlyphic Letter\nProvided: Glyphic Letter","desc":"I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from the kobold camps, ‹name›. It appears to be a letter sealed with the insignia of Khelden, our local mage trainer. I wouldn't hesitate to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hello, ‹name›. I am Khelden. Is there something I can do for you?","done":"Haha, I knew my note would not dissuade you from your path. So, you're prepared then, are you? Prepared to accept your fate? Prepared to challenge the gods and any other forces that stand before you in the pursuit of knowledge and power?\nI will not lie, ‹name›, you will be feared as much as respected. But also know this, I will be here for you when you need training. Simply seek me out as you grow more powerful.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.9,"y":41.6,"n":"Marshal McBride","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":49.7,"y":39.4,"n":"Khelden Bremen","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"9104":{"id":9104,"t":"Plagueheart Leggings","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Mataus the Wrathcaster at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Plagueheart Leggings if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Leggings, 20 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 4 Mooncloth and 2 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Leggings\n20 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Mooncloth\n2 Nexus Crystal","desc":"I make no pretenses, maggot. The darkness Plagueheart items hold could very well destroy the both of us. That is why the price is so high. If I'm going to die, it's going to be as a rich man.\nAnd I don't give an ounce of gnoll spit how you die, only that you do as I ask. Bring me what I require and we will both benefit - or die; but I've already explained this...","rew":"You will receive:\nPlagueheart Leggings\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Plagueheart Leggings.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.7,"n":"Mataus the Wrathcaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"3504":{"id":3504,"t":"Betrayed","lv":53,"min":44,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Sealed Letter to Ag'tor to Ag'tor Bloodfist in Azshara.\nSealed Letter to Ag'tor\nProvided: Sealed Letter to Ag'tor","desc":"Betraying, thieving woman! That's what I call her--that's all she'll ever be!\nI may have made a grave mistake, ‹name›. I trusted a blood elf. What's worse, I trusted a woman!\nShe claimed Azshara would hold great riches... powerful items. I simply send some warriors with her to protect her and I would be rewarded. Well, look who's the fool--she's killed them all.\nI want vengeance, ‹name›, but I can't afford to send anyone else. Find Ag'tor at Valormok, north of the Haldarr Encampment. He'll tell you more.","rew":"Experience: 2,650\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Ah, Belgrom wizened up and finally sent someone not in his ranks to aid us, did he?\nThis camp used to be a dozen warriors strong, ‹name›, but now they're all dead. That mage, Rimtori, has slain them all. She played Belgrom like a lute... seduced him even. It's none of my business, but between you and I, she is quite the temptress. That's probably why I'm still out here helping Belgrom--I probably would have done the same thing.","done":"We've sent everything we had at her and her workers, but they are strong in battle. None have bothered to return. I'm assuming some have died, but I'm sure others simply ran... cowards.\nBut now that reinforcements have arrived, perhaps there's still something we can do. Perhaps we can still punish her for lying and betraying Belgrom.\nWhat do you say, are you in?\nOrgrimmar Azshara","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":75.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Belgrom Rockmaul","s":1},{"z":"Azshara","x":22.3,"y":51.5,"n":"Ag'tor Bloodfist","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"7824":{"id":7824,"t":"A Donation of Runecloth","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"‹name›, you've been a tremendous contributor to our cloth drive. As we work hard to replenish our reserves, one form of cloth remains critically low - runecloth. We are in absolutely dire need of runecloth, and we hope that you will be able to help us as you have in the past.\nIf you are willing, please bring me what runecloth you can spare. We'll initially accept a single donation of sixty, and then we'll go from there.","done":"Fantastic - these will go right to use, I assure you. Thank you again for your assistance! We'd certainly be lost without you.\nWith all the donations you've made, I would certainly process any additional runecloth donations you care to make in the future. Just be sure to check in with me, and I'll personally make sure that your good deeds won't go unrecognized!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":63.6,"y":51.2,"n":"Rashona Straglash","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"8944":{"id":8944,"t":"Just Compensation","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Belt of Valor and a set of Gauntlets of Valor to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.\nBelt of Valor Patchwork Horror 3.3 % in Stratholme , Venom Belcher 3 % in Stratholme , Bile Spewer 2.7 % in Stratholme , Smolderthorn Berserker 2 %\nGauntlets of Valor Ramstein the Gorger 12 %","desc":"You've proven to be a very reliable individual, ‹name›. As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.\nFor now I will exchange your belt and gauntlets. If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.","rew":"You will receive:\nBelt of Heroism Gauntlets of Heroism\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're ready to perform the exchange?","done":"Our agreement remains in place. Just remember, this is but a taste of what awaits you. Free me of this cursed fate and I will reward you with items of truly great power.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"144":{"id":144,"t":"Messenger to Westfall","lv":14,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Magistrate Solomon with Gryan Stoutmantle's response.\nStoutmantle's Response to Solomon\nProvided: Stoutmantle's Response to Solomon","desc":"Magistrate Solomon's note pains me to read. But it is obvious he knows not the war which is waged in Westfall or else he would know better than to expect aid from the Militia. If Stormwind had not deserted us as well, we would not have the need for the Militia.\nTake this response to your master in Redridge, ‹class›. And let him know that my heart is heavy with the loss of good men.","rew":"Money: 1 50 0 gold, 1 silver, 50 copper Experience: 250\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Shall we expect the People's Militia soon? Does Lord Stoutmantle's news bode well?","done":"I do say, this is not good at all. I did not realize that Stoutmantle's situation was not unlike ours here in Lakeshire. What action is so important that it calls the Stormwind Army away from its people? Bah, I should not ponder aloud.\nHere, messenger. Accept these coins in exchange for your service to the Township. I might call upon you again.\nWestfall Redridge Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":56.3,"y":47.5,"n":"Gryan Stoutmantle","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.9,"y":44.5,"n":"Magistrate Solomon","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"96784":{"id":96784,"t":"Master of disguise","lv":34,"min":24,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"While disguised as a member of the Syndicate, find someone inside Stromgarde Keep who knows about the secret deal.\nSyndicate Uniform","desc":"<You recall Myrokos' instructions to find out about an important deal going on with the Syndicate in Stromgarde Keep. With your disguise, you should be able to talk to members of the Syndicate somewhat freely. Surely, one of them knows something.>\nLevel 34 , requires level 24 Difficulty 24 30 32 37 43 Side Both factions Class Rogue Quest ID 96784","cats":["rogue"]},"9024":{"id":9024,"t":"Aristan's Hunch","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Cologne Bottle and 1 Perfume Bottle to Morgan Pestle in the Trade District of Stormwind.\nCologne Bottle sold by Innkeeper Allison , sold by Innkeeper Firebrew , sold by Innkeeper Saelienne , sold by Innkeeper Gryshka and 4 more\nPerfume Bottle sold by Innkeeper Allison , sold by Innkeeper Firebrew , sold by Innkeeper Saelienne , sold by Innkeeper Gryshka and 4 more","desc":"I've got it! Have you smelled the new fragrance on the wind? The new colognes and perfumes that have come into fashion? Our guards wouldn't neglect their duties so easily.\nThat is, unless their thinking has been clouded by some foul alchemy.\nThere is only one way to be sure - bring a bottle of cologne and perfume to Morgan Pestle, and tell him my suspicions. I will reimburse you for their purchase when you return.","back":"Something I can help you with?","done":"I understand Aristan's concerns, but I really think he's overreacting. Let young men and women do what they will. I think Aristan has forgotten what it means to be young and in love.\nBut it would be better not to tell him that. We'll humor him.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":61.9,"y":75,"n":"Aristan Mottar","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":63.2,"y":74.4,"n":"Morgan Pestle","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"7024":{"id":7024,"t":"Great-father Winter is Here!","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Greatfather Winter; he is located near the Smokywood Pastures vendor area in Orgrimmar.","desc":"Have a wondrous Winter Veil, friend! Be sure to say hello to Greatfather Winter, who's currently in Orgrimmar! If you've been nice this year, you'll receive wondrous treats on the day of the Feast of Winter Veil. Be sure to tell him what you hope to get this year!\nAlso, be sure to stock up on treats to give those who've been nice this year. We have a great selection to choose from. Fresh from our farm to your plate - it's Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness!","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"Ho ho hello. I am Greatfather Winter, and I - courtesy of the fine folks of Smokywood Pastures... \"Fresh from our farm to your plate, it's Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness\" - would like to wish you a fantastic Feast of Winter Veil.\nIf you've been good this year, maybe you will receive treats from Smokywood Pastures as your treat for the Feast of Winter Veil. Huzzah.\nUndercity Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":68.2,"y":38.9,"n":"Nardstrum Copperpinch","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.4,"y":31.6,"n":"Greatfather Winter","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8304":{"id":8304,"t":"Dearest Natalia","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus wants you to question the inhabitants of Bronzebeard's Encampment. You will find Bronzebeard's Encampment south of Cenarion Hold.\nOnce you have gathered the requested information, return to Commander Mar'alith.\nFrankal Questioned\nRutgar Questioned","desc":"My dear Natalia has gone missing.\nTruth be told, she had been acting strangely for weeks leading up to her disappearance. I had caught her talking to herself when no one was around on more than one occasion. She was adamant that everything was ok and that she must be allowed to continue her research.\nShe was last seen heading to Bronzebeard's camp to the south.\nMy soldiers are spread too thin, ‹name›. I need you to go to Bronzebeard's camp and question those dwarves.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Waste no time, ‹name›!","done":"<Commander Mar'alith lowers his head in contemplation.>\nWhether she is alive or dead, I must do what is right. She must be found. Alas, I am bound by duty to this outpost. Will you help me once more, ‹name›?","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"1264":{"id":1264,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":33,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Commander Samaul in Dustwallow Marsh.","desc":"The beginning of every month the Kul Tiras Marines all get paid and usually leave Theramore for somewhere else. A lot of them come here to womanize, carouse, and just have a good time. One of those groups I'd consider regulars here at the tavern, and I believe this Hendel is among them.\nCommander Samaul in Theramore would be able to help you find him if Hendel's still stationed there. He's completely loyal to Proudmoore, but if you drop Elling's name, he should help you out... discreetly.","rew":"Experience: 1,300\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"A pleasure to meet you, ‹name›. I am Commander Samaul. I'm in charge of Miss Proudmoore's forces here in Theramore.\nAlthough I'm quite busy, if you have any questions, please feel free to speak up. I might have to keep it short, but there's no reason for me to be rude if you need my help.\nIf you plan on traveling out of the city, I'd suggest you be careful. Besides ogres, orcs and murlocs, the southern part of the swamp is filled with black dragons.\nWetlands Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.6,"y":60.8,"n":"Mikhail","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":68,"y":48.7,"n":"Commander Samaul","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"624":{"id":624,"t":"Cortello's Riddle","lv":43,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Solve the riddle!","desc":"There is an ornate, well-traveled bridge\nEast of Deadwind and south of Redridge\nUnderneath there waits something for you\nSome call it a hint, others a clue\nThere it will lie for endless tomorrows\nBiding its time in the Swamp of Sorrows","rew":"Experience: 3,600","done":"The soggy parchment contains the next clue....\nStranglethorn Vale Swamp of Sorrows","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":29.2,"y":88.3,"n":"Cortello's Riddle","s":1},{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":22.9,"y":48.2,"n":"A Soggy Scroll","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8064":{"id":8064,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Haruspex's Belt","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,500, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Bring Maywiki of Zuldazar a Primal Hakkari Sash. Maywiki of Zuldazar is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale. You must also be Honored with Zandalar.\nPrimal Hakkari Sash\nReach 9000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"We Zandalar know not of druidic ways; nature is to be shaped by our need, not the other way around. Still, a haruspex is the one of us most in tune with nature, and rightly so. To give up the ghost of a beastie is to know what it is to be one of them. That is the real power of nature.\nBring me an offerin' of the Paragons of Power from inside Zul'Gurub, proving yourself to us. Do this, and I'll give ya a powerful item - a belt used by many of the Zandalar's haruspices.\nStrong mojo, ya mon!","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Haruspex's Belt\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Got the Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub I need? The haruspex's belt will be yours if ya have them.","done":"I thank you - the latent power in these items will be treasures unto themselves, you betcha. Not only have ya done as I've asked of ya, but you've also proven to be honorable to us here in the tribe. As promised, here is your reward!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16,"n":"Maywiki of Zuldazar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1424":{"id":1424,"t":"Pool of Tears","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fel'zerul in Stonard wants you to gather 10 Atal'ai Artifacts.\n10 Atal'ai Artifact Atal'ai Artifact , Atal'ai Artifact , Atal'ai Artifact","desc":"The Warchief sent us to investigate strange happenings at The Temple of Atal'Hakkar.\nThe Atal'ai trolls are a tribe of dark casters, known for practicing forbidden magic. You can imagine how astonished we were when we arrived here to discover the temple had been sunk.\nThe green dragons now guard the site, claiming to be protectors of Azeroth.\nWe need to discover what happened. Explore around the Pool of Tears and gather Atal'ai artifacts. From those I can begin to piece together this puzzle.","rew":"Money: 1 20 1 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,450\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"No one knows what dark practices went on inside The Temple of Atal'Hakkar. But we do know that great and powerful forces of magic were used.\nWe must learn as much as we can about such magic. Perhaps the spells of the Atal'ai will prove of use to the Horde.\nOnce you have gathered enough Atal'ai artifacts from around the Pool of Tears, I can begin to understand what the trolls were hoping to accomplish and what went so horribly wrong.","done":"Your diligence in collecting the Atal'ai artifacts is worthy of praise, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":47.9,"y":54.8,"n":"Fel'zerul","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"6384":{"id":6384,"t":"Ride to Orgrimmar","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Buy a wind rider to Orgrimmar from the wind rider master Devrak, then bring Zargh's Meats to Gryshka in Orgrimmar.\nZargh's Meats\nProvided: Zargh's Meats","desc":"For just a few coins I will have a wind rider bring you to Orgrimmar. When you get there, you can take Zargh's Meats to Gryshka. Her inn is in the Valley of Strength, not far from the Skytower, where my wind rider will drop you off.\nSpeak with me again when you are ready for the journey.","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 420\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+50 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Something smells good! You don't have raw meat on you, do you?","done":"Oh, wonderful! Those are fine cuts! These are from Zargh, are they? That orc sure knows his way into a lady's heart...\nOh, I can't wait to cook it. But not too much! Meat is best served rare, don't you think?\nThe Barrens Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.5,"y":30.3,"n":"Devrak","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":54.1,"y":68.4,"n":"Innkeeper Gryshka","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1104":{"id":1104,"t":"Salt Flat Venom","lv":30,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Salty Scorpid Venoms to Fizzle Brassbolts in the Shimmering Flats.\n6 Salty Scorpid Venom Scorpid Terror 10 % , Scorpid Reaver 10 % , Vile Sting 10 %","desc":"I have so many designs for our rocket car! So many! And I must try them all!!\nI'm working on a new type of fuel. One that burns really really really hot!! I haven't gotten the mixture perfect, but I think I know what I need...\nThe scorpids who wander the Shimmering Flats have a venom with lots and lots of salt in it. It's very unique! And it's just what I need!\nBring me venom and trust me -- our car will fly!!","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,850","back":"Hi hi hi! Did you get that venom??","done":"All right! This venom is going to work great! Thanks, ‹name›!\nNow I just need to boil it down, apply skipper-otomer, add a nega-catalyst, and... Drat! Where are my notes!?","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":78.1,"y":77.1,"n":"Fizzle Brassbolts","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1184":{"id":1184,"t":"Parts of the Swarm","lv":35,"min":28,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Belgrom Rockmaul in Orgrimmar.","desc":"Head back to Belgrom in Orgrimmar and tell him Moktar be doing his bidding well out in the Thousand Needles. Tell him also, that me studies progress, and I hope to be havin' learned more soon. That should please him greatly.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDryleaf Pants Bleeding Crescent\nMoney: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,350\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"I'm appreciative of your efforts, ‹class›. The warchief will enjoy hearing how tenacious you have been in your duties.\nOh, of course I will mention your name to him. He speaks to me often and values my opinions greatly.\nGo now, I have much to do. And if you speak to Korran soon, and he has news of these creatures, then return to me--I would think they are a threat that must be taken seriously.\nThe Barrens Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.1,"y":29.6,"n":"Korran","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":75.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Belgrom Rockmaul","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"86784":{"id":86784,"t":"Sticks and bones","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 6 Dry Branches and bring them to Eleanor Shackleton.\n6 Dry Branch","desc":"My associate Eleanor Shackleton prides herself on traveling the wilds, surviving against weather and monsters. She is currently camped not far from here, in the hills to the west, and I remember a piece of advice that she once gave me: \"When you think you have enough firewood, gather five times more.\"\nIf you have some spare time, you could collect some wood in this basket and take it to her camp. I'm sure she could give you a few tips about the existence of a traveling adventurer.","rew":"You will receive:\nCollecting Basket\nMoney: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Welcome to my fire, traveler.","done":"Extra firewood? That is always welcome. It will keep these old bones warm through the cold nights of the Glades.\nI have a sling for collecting wood myself, so you might as well hang onto that basket.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":58.4,"y":51.4,"n":"Deathguard Bartholomew","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.2,"y":55.4,"n":"Eleanor Shackleton","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"704":{"id":704,"t":"Agmond's Fate","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Restorer's Fine Gloves, Excavator Gauntlets.","obj":"Bring 4 Carved Stone Urns to Prospector Ironband in Loch Modan.\n4 Carved Stone Urn Carved Stone Urn","desc":"The last report I received from Agmond is troubling, more so now that he's dead! He mentioned that his diggers uncovered \"ancient urns\" at the dig site outside Uldaman. I fear that the urns he found at that site incited the troggs, just as did the idols I found here.\nI need you to get those urns for our studies. Go to the Uldaman site, gather the urns, then return to me.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nProspector Gloves Restorer's Fine Gloves Excavator Gauntlets\nNew in Forever: Restorer's Fine Gloves, Excavator Gauntlets.\nExperience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Did you find those urns, ‹name›? We must find the link between them and the troggs!","done":"Well done! With luck and diligence, we will find whatever link exists between the troggs and these ancient artifacts.\nYou have done a great deed for the Prospectors, ‹name›. Your efforts will not be forgotten. And neither will Agmond.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":65.9,"y":65.6,"n":"Prospector Ironband","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"4144":{"id":4144,"t":"Bloodpetal Sprouts","lv":53,"min":47,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Bloodpetal Sprout Stone Guardian , Tar Creeper , Tar Lord , Tar Beast and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 3,950","back":"Here's the plan, ‹name›: Go out and collect some bloodpetal sprouts -- you know, the plants that haven't fully sprouted yet, and bring them here. Then I'll see what the Atal'ai haze can do.\nYou may think I'm vengeful... Actually, you'd be right about that!\nTruth is, I know the way out of here, but until Larion will admit that I'm right, I'm staying right here!\nSo off with you, find those bloodpetal sprouts and let's have some fun!","done":"Here goes nothing, ‹name›! This will get Larion's attention!","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":42.9,"y":9.6,"n":"Muigin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4384":{"id":4384,"t":"Crystal Yield","lv":53,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Red Power Crystal Red Power Crystal , Red Power Crystal , Mor'vek 46.2 % , Stegodon 0.4 % and 4 more\n10 Blue Power Crystal Blue Power Crystal , Blue Power Crystal , Mor'vek 25.6 % , Plated Stegodon 0.3 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n6 Crystal Yield","back":"The Pylon table allows you to combine red power crystals with blue power crystals.\nAccording to J.D.'s manual, this combination can be used to weaken an enemy's defenses.","done":"Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.\nThe resulting combination is now yours.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":23.9,"y":59.2,"n":"Western Crystal Pylon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"864":{"id":864,"t":"Return to Apothecary Zinge","lv":46,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Sealed Field Testing Kit to Apothecary Zinge in the Undercity.\nSealed Field Testing Kit\nProvided: Sealed Field Testing Kit","desc":"\"Here you go, the power source is safely removed and the data is preserved. Well, safe journeys and all that. Hope the nefarious science experiment worked out for you and all.\"\nThe goblin turns away from you to attend to the demands of the Gadgetzan Water Company. You secure the sealed testing kit for the journey back to the Undercity. Apothecary Zinge waits for you and the sealed field testing kit there.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSkilled Handling Gloves Master Apothecary Cape Loreskin Shoulders\nMoney: 1 30 1 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,050\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"Welcome back. At least, welcome back if you have returned with a sealed testing kit. Otherwise, I will pretend not to notice your utter incompetence and spare my wrath from you until you do as you have been tasked and accomplish my task.","done":"I will analyze this data immediately. Perhaps Keever's insanity will prove to be my genius after all.\nAs for you... you are useful to me, and I reward quite well those who remain useful. Take this item, this coin, and most importantly my thanks along with them.\nCheck back with me from time to time - I wager that our working together on this project is not at an end.\nTanaris Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":28.5,"n":"Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":50.1,"y":68,"n":"Apothecary Zinge","e":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"1504":{"id":1504,"t":"The Binding","lv":11,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Using the Glyphs of Summoning, summon and subdue a voidwalker, then return the Glyphs of Summoning to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.\nSummoned Voidwalker slain\nProvided: Glyphs of Summoning","desc":"Now, observe the Tablet of Verga, for it contains the glyphs you will need for the summoning. Take them to the circle in Neeru Fireblade's tent on the other side of the cavern. There you will be able to call for the voidwalker.\nYou must defeat it using whatever physical and magical means you have at your disposal. When this is completed, return to me with the glyphs of summoning and I will demonstrate how you may bind the creature to your will.","rew":"You will learn: Summon Voidwalker\nExperience: 650","back":"The voidwalker is a powerful creature. I remember when it was I that was in your shoes, ‹name›. Over the years, my own voidwalker has grown to fight me less, though I suspect that is only because it hopes I will let my guard down.\nRemember that, ‹name›.","done":"You have done well, ‹name›. I will show you how to summon the voidwalker similar to the one you just defeated.\nYou should know that we have high expectations for you, and you have, so far, matched them.\nDo not let it go to your head, however, as the tasks that still lie before you will make this seem as simple as waking in the morning.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.2,"y":45.3,"n":"Gan'rul Bloodeye","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4784":{"id":4784,"t":"Components for the Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe","lv":37,"min":31,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring some Fine Gold Thread, 2 Smoldering Coals, and a Soul Shard to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.\nFine Gold Thread\n2 Smoldering Coal Burning Exile 30 %\nSoul Shard sold by Jimmy McWeaksauce","desc":"I need only three things now, ‹name›, then we can finish your robe.\nFirst, the fine gold thread Xizk is making for you. Return to him in Booty Bay and get it.\nSecond, bring me two smoldering coals from the fire elementals in the Arathi Highlands. If I recall correctly, they are to the west, near Thoradin's Wall.\nFinally, a soul shard created by you.\nAfter you have all the components, return here to the tower and I will complete the robe for you.","rew":"Experience: 2,100","back":"Soon, ‹name›. I promise you. The robe will be more than adequate for your needs and certainly give you an edge over your opponents.","done":"Excellent, ‹name›! The components are gathered and we are ready.\nI trust you will be pleased.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1824":{"id":1824,"t":"Trial at the Field of Giants","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 twitching antennae to Ruga Ragetotem at Camp Taurajo\n5 Twitching Antenna Silithid Harvester , Silithid Creeper , Silithid Grub , Silithid Swarmer and 1 more","desc":"To pass this trial, you must travel south to the Field of Giants. There you will find a host of crawling, insect creatures. They are new to the Barrens and I do not like what they herald.\nBring me their still-twitching antennae, and waste no time, ‹name›, for harvested antennae will not twitch for long. Bring me the antennae in the time allowed, and you will pass the trial.","rew":"You will receive:\nRuga's Bulwark\nExperience: 1,550","back":"Do you have the antennae? If so then give them to me quickly, for twitching antennae do not twitch forever...","done":"Nicely done, ‹name›! In passing the trial at the Field of Giants, you take one more step down the warrior's path.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.7,"y":59.4,"n":"Ruga Ragetotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"5904":{"id":5904,"t":"A Plague Upon Thee","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find someplace suitable in the center of the Northridge Lumber Mill in Western Plaguelands to place the Barrel of Plagueland Termites.\nProvided: Barrel of Plagueland Termites","desc":"Now that we have the termites, take this steel reinforced barrel to the Northridge Lumber Mill south of Hearthglen--you'll find it to the west of the road that leads you up to the town.\nOnce there, place the barrel in the center of the lumber mill; find someplace suitable, like on a crate and then open it. The termites should do their work from there and make the mill useless to the Crusade.","rew":"Experience: 2,800","done":"The termites are obviously getting restless as you place the barrel on top of the crate.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43.4,"y":84.8,"n":"Nathaniel Dumah","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":48.3,"y":32,"n":"Termite Barrel","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5504":{"id":5504,"t":"Mantles of the Dawn","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Argent Dawn Valor Tokens to Quartermaster Hasana at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\n10 Argent Dawn Valor Token\nReach 21000 reputation with Argent Dawn","desc":"Your service to the Argent Dawn is to be commended, ‹name›. You are truly revered amongst us. I have been authorized to make available for you to purchase one of the Dawn's most valued items - our magic resistance mantles.\nApplication of a mantle to your existing shoulder piece will enhance your resistance to the powers of magic in one of five potential ways. As a sign of continued dedication to our cause, I ask for no less than ten of our valor tokens in exchange for access to these mantles.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Ah, noble ‹class›! Have you brought the valor tokens requested of you? Once you hand them to me, I will make our various mantles available to you for purchase.","done":"Outstanding - your tribute to the Dawn is duly noted, ‹name›. With this accomplished, I am delighted to make our mantles available to you for purchase. So long as you maintain your current status with us, these mantles will be purchasable from any authorized quartermaster of the Argent Dawn.\nFor the Dawn, my brother/sister!","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.3,"y":68.1,"n":"Argent Quartermaster Hasana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5344":{"id":5344,"t":"The Last Barov","lv":60,"min":52,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,300 experience instead of 8,800, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Travel to the Bulwark - Horde territory - and assassinate Alexi Barov. Take his head and return to Weldon Barov.\nBe warned, Alexi will probably be well protected by Horde filth.\nHead of Alexi Barov Alexi Barov","desc":"With the deeds recovered, there is but one thing left to do. Alexi must be killed. With him dead, I need not ever worry about an unscrupulous gang of mercenaries seeking my head.\nIt's a simple task. Alexi hides under the protection of the Horde - at the Bulwark.\nNo, I do not expect you to just walk up and kill him, I want his head! How you get it... well, that part is up to you. That type of behavior is below one of my noble upbringing.","rew":"You will receive:\nBarov Peasant Caller\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300","back":"You do want payment, do you not?","done":"A glorious day it is! Finally, the pockmark of house Barov eliminated and my fortune secure!\nTake this and leave my sight, peasant.\nWestern Plaguelands Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43.5,"y":83.7,"n":"Weldon Barov","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"64":{"id":64,"t":"The Forgotten Heirloom","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Farmer Furlbrow wants you to retrieve his pocket watch from the wardrobe in his farmhouse at the pumpkin farm to the West.\nFurlbrow's Pocket Watch Furlbrow's Wardrobe","desc":"It was horrible! Verna woke me when she heard a ruckus in the fields. The fields were full of hooligans. We left in a rush and I forgot to pack my pocket watch. Verna's pa gave me that watch on our wedding day and I feel just sick knowing those thieves have it. I left the pocket watch in the wardrobe at the farmhouse. Look for the field of pumpkins to the West -- you can't miss it. If you bring it back to me, I'd sure be grateful!","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Freshly Baked Bread 10 Ice Cold Milk\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Don't suppose you were able to get my watch?","done":"My watch! Thank you so much, kind sir!\nWe are but poor farmers and we have lost our land but please accept this reward as a token of our appreciation.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":60,"y":19.4,"n":"Farmer Furlbrow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"464":{"id":464,"t":"War Banners","lv":28,"min":23,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 25s instead of 20s.","obj":"Bring 8 Dragonmaw War Banners to Captain Stoutfist.\n8 Dragonmaw War Banner Chieftain Nek'rosh 80 % , Dragonmaw Bonewarder 80 % , Dragonmaw Shadowwarder 80 % , Dragonmaw Centurion 80 % and 3 more","desc":"The Dragonmaw orc clan was all but destroyed by the end of the Second War, after they lost control of their red dragon pets. The dragons were not very happy with their old masters, and fiercely hunted the Dragonmaws. What few remained fled from Grim Batol and into the Mountains east of Whelgar's Excavation.\nNow they've gained strength, and have an encampment northeast of Menethil.\nWe want you to attack that encampment. Gather and bring me their war banners as proof.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,300\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Have you attacked the Dragonmaw encampment?","done":"Well fought, ‹name›. The Dragonmaws are not the same threat they were when they had dragons, but they're still fierce opponents.\nThe Dragonmaws are led by Nek'rosh, son of Nekros, who was the former head of the Dragonmaws years ago. Nekros used powerful magic to tame the Red Dragons, but when that magic failed him...the dragons were not happy.\nNekros was killed, and his son has vowed revenge against the dragons who slew his father.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":9.9,"y":57.5,"n":"Captain Stoutfist","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"304":{"id":304,"t":"A Grim Task","lv":34,"min":26,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Fury Ring.","obj":"Kill Balgaras the Foul and bring his ear to Longbraid the Grim outside of Dun Modr.\nEar of Balgaras Balgaras the Foul","desc":"Many of my soldiers died in the battle of Dun Modr. My own brother perished when the West Bridge over the Thandol Span was destroyed. Aye, the Dark Iron dwarves are a devilish breed. From what Roggo was able to gather, the leader of the thugs in the Wetlands is a warlock named Balgaras the Foul. He is quite a coward, sending his soldiers to do his bidding but hides in his camp on Direforge Hill, to the southeast.\nIf you can find the spineless scum, slay him and bring me his ear. I will reward you, ‹class›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGold Lion Shield Tranquil Ring Fury Ring\nNew in Forever: Fury Ring.\nExperience: 3,350\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Were you able to locate Balgaras the Foul yet, ‹class›? He has been evading us for quite some time.","done":"Balgaras the Foul is finally dead. While his death will not bring back the many innocent dwarves who died needlessly by his hand, it will help to restore peace of mind to those who survived. With Balgaras dead, the remaining Dark Iron scum should be easy enough to manage. Now, we must wipe them out before a new leader is sent to these parts.\nYou have done well, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":49.8,"y":18.3,"n":"Longbraid the Grim","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"4864":{"id":4864,"t":"Enraged Wildkin","lv":59,"min":53,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Pick up Jaron's Supplies from the snow, then find the wildkin that stole the amulet Jaron spoke of.\nBring Jaron's Supplies and the Blue-feathered Amulet to Jaron Stoneshaper at the lodge in Winterspring.\nJaron's Supplies Jaron's Supplies , Jaron's Supplies\nBlue-feathered Amulet Berserk Owlbeast , Moontouched Owlbeast , Crazed Owlbeast","desc":"After inspecting the contents of the box, you decide that Jaron could make use of the tools and other items inside. However, there is no sign of the amulet.\nIt appears that the wildkin inhabit the lands to the north and east of here, so you decide that the next step is to face the creatures and reclaim the amulet from them.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,400\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Aye... Tell me the news.","done":"Well, I expected to hear as much, lad. I figured that the crazed beasts destroyed all of my belongings...\nBut you did find my tools, and most importantly, the amulet! I wonder why the wildkin so fiercely defended this item... In any case, I'll think twice before heading their way again!","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.4,"y":60.7,"n":"Jaron's Wagon","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":52.1,"y":30.4,"n":"Jaron Stoneshaper","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"92464":{"id":92464,"t":"Elemental unrest","lv":3,"min":2,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to the Yala Windwatcher in Thendal Grove.\nLearn more about the agitated winds.","desc":"Ever since our elemental benefactors left us, it seems that we are simply moving from one unrest to another. The problem we face now is that the manifestations of the winds near the standing stones to the northeast are agitated.\nNot truly self-aware like the sentient wind spirits that once lived here, these simple sprites respond in kind to forces, emotions, and intentions of the creatures around them.\nMy apprentice Yala Windwatcher went to observe them. Seek her out and discover what she's learned.","done":"Rorian sent you? Good. I could use your aid.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42,"y":23.4,"n":"Rorian the Dayseeker","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":47.2,"y":21.8,"n":"Yala Windwatcher","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92544":{"id":92544,"t":"Alaketh thugs","lv":5,"min":2,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 6 Al'Aketh Brutes, 4 Al'Aketh Neophytes, and Malduko Cloudcrush in Thendal Grove.\nAl'Aketh Brute slain : 0/ 6\nAl'Aketh Neophyte slain : 0/ 4\nMalduko Cloudcrush slain","desc":"A band of Al'Aketh cult ruffians have taken up residence near the temple ruins just southwest of here, led by a real monster called Malduko Cloudcrush. This rabble has no doubt been dispatched here by High Priestess Lorthuna at the Shrine of Akir to attack travelers and coerce our people into joining the cult.\nI need to stay here at my post to alert travelers leaving the grove of the danger, but I would be grateful if you could do something about those cultists and their leader for me.","done":"It was all I could do to stop myself from going over and joining you from my position here. I can only hope that these louts got the message and clear out of here soon.\nThank you, ‹class›. You have the gratitude of the Rangers of Thendal Grove.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":38.2,"y":30.2,"n":"Hanaa Nightwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"2864":{"id":2864,"t":"Tran'rek","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Tran'rek in Gadgetzan.","desc":"My cousin Tran'rek is in a tight spot. He promised me a load of scarab shells weeks ago and he hasn't delivered. He's my cousin, so I'd hate to have to send someone to Gadgetzan to break something on him.\nCan you speak to Tran'rek for me? Let him know he needs to get that delivery together before I do something rash?\nGadgetzan is in northern Tanaris, in Kalimdor.","rew":"Experience: 390\n+25 reputation with Gadgetzan","done":"Hello!\nOh, you spoke to my cousin Krazek? How is he? I hope Booty Bay is treating him well...\nScarab shells, you say? Well... let me tell you a story...\nStranglethorn Vale Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.9,"y":77.2,"n":"Krazek","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.6,"y":26.8,"n":"Tran'rek","e":1}],"cats":["zulfarrak"]},"8144":{"id":8144,"t":"Zandalarian Shadow Mastery Talisman","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Zandalarian Shadow Talisman","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalarian Shadow Mastery Talisman\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"It yearns to grow, ‹name›. The talisman has soaked in all that you have done. The thousands of troll corpses littering Zul'Gurub have fueled its power. Hand it to me and I shall make the final enhancement.","done":"This is the last time we will speak under the auspices of Shera Ali'kh. You know all that you must. Take the talisman and continue in your slaying. Hakkar must never be allowed to leave Zul'Gurub.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.1,"y":13.7,"n":"Falthir the Sightless","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});